  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've been using a face camera on my avatar for years now, and I'm looking forward to being able to switch to an official feature for it, and take back the material and mesh it costs in my perf stats. As part of this, however, I'd really appreciate it if I could fine-tune the near and far clip planes to adjust exactly the range of distances that appear in the camera.\nIn my current avatar-camera based implementation, I've adjusted things so that the far clip plane is relatively far from the camera, a few cm from my face. This means that it doesn't show other people who are at a normal distance for talking, but if I'm being headpatted that does appear. I've also configured it to over-render the world (ZTest Always) to avoid issues with it clipping through random objects.\nHere's hoping the new official implementation has the configurability I'd need to remove my avatar-based setup!",
